list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48745","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56664","marks":["bold"],"text":"Specifications"}]},{"id":"blk-48746","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48748","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56665","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"OS-011 — Embodiment Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-48747","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48750","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56666","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"OS-E001 — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning"}]}],"id":"blk-48749","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48751","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56667","marks":["bold"],"text":"UX & build prompts"}]},{"id":"blk-48752","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56668","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ux/user-stories-embodiment.md"}],"text":"Embodiment (body-browser + body-os) — User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-48753","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56669","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/prompts/OS-008-BUILD.md"}],"text":"OS-008 Agent Harness Protocol — Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-48755","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48757","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56670","text":"The Three Enforcement Layers"}]},{"id":"blk-48758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56671","text":"OpenSentience provides three layers of runtime enforcement:"}]},{"id":"blk-48759","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OS-008 Harness:   \"Has this agent followed the correct process?\"\n                   Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts\n\nOS-006 Shim:      \"Is this agent allowed to do this?\"\n                   Permissions, lifecycle, autonomy levels\n\nOS-007 Security:  \"Is this agent under attack?\"\n                   Threat detection, identity verification, circuit breakers"},{"id":"blk-48760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56672","text":"All three log to the same append-only audit trail, creating a unified compliance record from protocol to permission to pipeline."}]},{"id":"blk-48761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56673","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48762","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56674","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-48763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56675","text":"Above the cognitive primitives, OpenSentience publishes three sibling protocols that together turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate:"}]},{"id":"blk-48764","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009) — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010) — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&] Protocol     — composes capabilities     structural│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-48766","spans":[{"id":"spn-56676","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-48767","spans":[{"id":"spn-56677","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-48768","spans":[{"id":"spn-56678","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-48765","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-48769","spans":[{"id":"spn-56679","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-48770","spans":[{"id":"spn-56680","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-48771","spans":[{"id":"spn-56681","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48772","spans":[{"id":"spn-56682","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-48773","spans":[{"id":"spn-56683","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-48774","spans":[{"id":"spn-56684","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-56685","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48775","spans":[{"id":"spn-56686","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-48776","spans":[{"id":"spn-56687","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-48777","spans":[{"id":"spn-56688","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-48778","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56689","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-56690","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-56691","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-56692","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-56693","text":" and its runtime passes the 12-test conformance suite. A system is "},{"id":"spn-56694","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-56695","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-56696","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-56697","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-56698","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-56699","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-56700","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-56701","text":" phase. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-48779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56702","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48780","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56703","text":"Relationship to the [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-48781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56704","text":"OpenSentience occupies the "},{"id":"spn-56705","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance and research layer"},{"id":"spn-56706","text":" of the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-48782","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  [&] Protocol        — capability composition (what an agent CAN do)\n  OpenSentience       — governance + harness (what an agent MAY do, and how)\n  Graphonomous        — memory + learning (OS-001, OS-002, OS-004, OS-005)\n  AgenTroMatic        — deliberation (OS-003)\n  Delegatic           — policy authoring (feeds into OS-006 enforcement)\n  Agentelic           — agent manifests (consumed by OS-006 install)\n  FleetPrompt         — marketplace (agents enter governance on install)\n  SpecPrompt          — acceptance criteria (consumed by OS-008 quality gates)"},{"id":"blk-48783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56707","text":"The governance shim wraps any OTP "},{"id":"spn-56708","marks":["code"],"text":"child_spec"},{"id":"spn-56709","text":". It does not replace the supervised process — it interposes permission checks, lifecycle management, autonomy control, pipeline enforcement, and audit logging around it."}]},{"id":"blk-48784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56710","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-48785","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56711","text":"Founding Thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-48786","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56712","text":"OpenSentience exists because intelligence without governance is generation without accumulation. The ten protocols formalize what structured accumulation requires: memory that consolidates, routing that detects cycles, deliberation that resolves conflict, attention that prioritizes, resources that adapt, governance that enforces boundaries, security that detects threats, a harness that orchestrates the entire pipeline, "},{"id":"spn-56713","marks":["bold"],"text":"diagnostics that measure whether the loop actually learns"},{"id":"spn-56714","text":" (PRISM), and a "},{"id":"spn-56715","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal manifest"},{"id":"spn-56716","text":" that lets every loop in the ecosystem declare how it cycles and signals (PULSE)."}]},{"id":"blk-48787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56717","text":"The shim is deliberately thin. Governance should cost less than 1% of the system it governs. PULSE is a manifest standard with no required runtime. PRISM runs as a separate benchmark engine that any system can opt into via its PULSE manifest."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierarp3bxkfiiu6wleichngwjwgzbxnmrgnm6drxc2bhvxtotyxln3jq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}